          "filename": "43-47 West 28th Street.jpg",
          "caption": "43 (right) - 47 (left) West 28th Street between Broadway and Sixth Avenue in the NoMad neighborhood of Manhattan, New York City, were built c.1915, c.1912, and c.1920, respectively.  In their heyday, these buildings were a part of Tin Pan Alley, and were filled with songwriters, music publishers and other elements of the music industry. (See File:Tinpanalley.jpg (thumbnail below) for the same three buildings when they were part of Tin Pan Alley)",
